INT. LAUNDROMAT - 3 A.M.

Fluorescent hum. One dryer turning, a single red sock tumbling.

NKEM OKPARA, 30s, in a hospital lanyard, stares at a folded child's pajama set. BARTHOLOMEW "BART" LENNOX, 60s, mop in hand, watches from the doorway.

BART
You been here since midnight. Machine two's been done since one.

NKEM
I know.

She does not move. Bart steps closer.

BART
Whose are they?

NKEM
(sudden, loud)
Mine! They were -- they're mine, I'm allowed to wash them!

She hurls the pajamas at the dryer. They slap the glass. Bart does not flinch.

BART
Nobody said you weren't.

NKEM
Stop being nice to me.

BART
Can't help it.

NKEM
I SAID --

BART ^
Okay.

NKEM
Stop!

Silence. The red sock turns. Nkem slides down the machine to the floor.

NKEM (CONT'D)
(quiet)
She's seven. She's fine. She's in a bed upstairs, and she's fine.

Bart sits on an upturned bucket.

BART
Then fold the rest.
